WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.170
 Billy, Robert,
congratulations.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.873
You've made it to the final
round of this competition.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.375
Now, we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:13.380
to recreate an iconic weapon
that helped win World War II--

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.821
the Scottish backsword.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:22.788
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:24.690
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:28.161 line:7%
[heavy metal music]

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:33.166
So it's day one, and
I'm going to get started

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:36.302
on my Scottish backsword.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:37.937
So right now, I'm
just cleaning off

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:42.108
my steel, just to make sure that
I get a good, clean forge weld.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.643
I don't have the steel
that's a proper thickness,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.280
so I'm going to be forge welding
three pieces of 1080 steel

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.347
together.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.815
I'm doing it all by
hand, so it's going

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:52.485
to take a little bit longer.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.056 line:7%
[heavy metal music]

00:00:57.356 --> 00:01:01.260
 So I'm making a
Scottish backsword.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.995
I'm going to try to
make it as historically

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:05.832
accurate as I possibly can.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:08.968
Let's make it hot.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.370
Day one is making
the Damascus, forging

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.439
the blade, and then quench.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.107
Woo, boy!

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.243
There's a risk that the
Damascus will blow apart.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.180
And if it messes up, I won't
have time to start again.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.117
Forge welding Damascus
is always a risky thing,

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.185
but it will make the blade
far more aesthetically

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.655
pleasing, which
will hopefully give

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.490
me a boost in this competition.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.725
Things are OK.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.926
I've got my blade
forged to shape.

00:01:33.992 --> 00:01:36.396
I'm ready to go in the quench.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:39.632
I can't believe I got
this much done in one day.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:45.738
I think that might have
been a successful quenching.

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:46.873
Coming out.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:47.640
Aha!

00:01:50.542 --> 00:01:52.745 line:0%
 So today, I have a
little bit of grinding

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:54.914 line:7%
left to establish my bevels.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.550
And then the plan after
that is heat treat.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.285
Once I come right
out of the quench,

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:03.256
I lay the sword down here,
clamp everything down tight.

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:04.757
And hopefully, if
there is any warp,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:08.628
it straightens it out
as the blade is cooling.

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:13.699
If things go wrong here, I could
possibly have to start over.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.901
I have to nail it and get
it right the first time.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:16.635
All right.

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:17.403
Here we go.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:27.012
I saw some good color when
it came out of the quench.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.548
The blade looked
fairly straight.

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.716
I didn't hear any thinks or
cracks or anything happen,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.551
so I think we're good.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:38.490
 My plan for today is
to make the basket hilt.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.493
It's easily the toughest
part of this build.

00:02:41.593 --> 00:02:43.730
I'm going to try my
best to make this thing

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.298
out of a single piece of steel.

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:49.135
That's why you drill it slow.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:50.803
I'm going to try to
put my own spin on it.

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:54.540
I want to put the American flag
and the shape of the Purple

00:02:54.606 --> 00:02:57.042
Heart medal to honor
the men and women who

00:02:57.142 --> 00:02:58.577
have given all to our country.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:00.713
At least as much work
is going into the handle

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.183
as is going into the blade.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:08.321
It can be a Scottish backsword
with an American touch.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:13.693 line:0%
Today, my main
focus is going to be

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:17.930 line:0%
on the hilt. To get this hilt
going, what I'm going to need

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:22.535 line:0%
to do is tack the guard and
quillon to the blade itself

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:25.305 line:0%
in order to start building
the basket around that.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.077
I'm very happy with
my progress so far.

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:33.312
I feel like I have
a real good shot.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.748
Hopefully it holds up to
whatever test they throw at me.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:44.389 line:0%
 Everything looks great,
but I've got one final touch

00:03:44.489 --> 00:03:46.292 line:7%
that I want to do to my weapon.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.928
I use a little purple, a little
gold, and a little silver,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:53.332
and I really brighten up the
image of the Purple Heart.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.301
She is a beautiful,
beautiful sword.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:58.604
What can I test it on?

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.239
I want to be the
first person to hack

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:01.640
something up with this thing.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:05.011
It just screams, go
out and swing me.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:08.314
But I'm not putting my blade
through a rigorous test here.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.282
I'm just seeing if
the edge is good.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:11.718
So I set up some swim noodles.

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:14.921
That'll do.

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.458
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.127
Captain Mad Jack Churchill may
have been mad enough to take

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:24.563
a backsword into modern combat.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.801
But what I want to know is,
are your swords mad enough

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.170
if called upon to kill?

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.839
To that end, I will
deliver some killing

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.940
blows to this ballistics dummy.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:35.975
Billy, you are first.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.343
You ready for this?

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.145
 I came here to watch you
kill and chew bubblegum,

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.646
and I'm out of bubblegum.

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:41.981
 All right.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:42.949
Let's do this.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:52.425
[heavy metal music]

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.912
All right, Billy.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:16.382
First up, I really like the
way the Damascus spatter

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.650
shows in your sword.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.987
Now, your handle--
it's comfortable.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:23.689
There are no hot spots.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:28.427
Every cut you do with this blade
is sharp enough to cut deeply.

00:05:28.493 --> 00:05:32.164
Overall, your weapon will kill.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.699
 Thank you very much.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.167
 All right, Robert.
Your turn, sir.

00:05:35.233 --> 00:05:36.268
Are you ready?
- I'm ready.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.003
 Let's do this.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:44.944
[suspenseful music]

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.104
I will not be denied.

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:16.175
All right, Robert.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.877
Let's talk about
your backsword here.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:23.349
The tip-- very pointy, thrust
in easily, cuts on the way out.

00:06:23.415 --> 00:06:25.284
Your handle here-- it's loose.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:27.353
It's really wiggling in my hand.

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:32.057
But overall, sir, your
backsword will kill.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:32.792
 Thank you.

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:38.798
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.632
Today, I'm going to
take your swords,

00:06:40.732 --> 00:06:43.436
and I'm a clear a path
through this big block of ice.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:45.671
And I don't really care what
your swords do to the ice.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.040
I want to see what the
ice does to your swords.

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:50.475
Billy, you look
ready to be first.

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:51.810
 Jay, I was born ready.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.145
 There we go.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.982
 The ice block is brutal.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.817
It can chip the edge of a blade.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.485
It can break a blade.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:02.221
I'm a little nervous
going into this.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.690
Nothing left to it but
to it but to do it.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:11.097
[heavy metal music]

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:33.952
 Billy, nice job.

00:07:34.019 --> 00:07:35.354
 Thank you.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.589
 I'm sure you could see when I
striking that, the blade flexed

00:07:37.656 --> 00:07:39.258
all over the place and
came right back to where

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:40.593
it was in the beginning.

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.227
Everything is tight.

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:43.161
Nice job.

00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:44.463
 Thank you very much.

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:45.664
 Robert, how you feeling?

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:46.865
- I'm ready.
- Good.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:47.399
I'm ready too.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:48.334
Let's do it.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.502
[suspenseful music]

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:53.306
 I'd be lying if I said
I'm not nervous right now.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:55.441
A sword isn't made to
hit a block of ice.

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:58.143
When two hard things hit
each other like that,

00:07:58.243 --> 00:07:59.678
something's got to give.

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:02.849
Hopefully, the ice gives
more than my sword gives.

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:12.825
[heavy metal music]

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:20.565
 Oh, no.

00:08:20.665 --> 00:08:23.268
I really don't know
what to think right now.

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:24.636
 This right here
is where it hurts.

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:25.971
It feels like something pulled.

00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:28.540
 Watching Jay scream
out in pain like that,

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:29.941
I feel that pain as well.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:33.312
 It's kind of catching
me a little bit back here.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.347
 I hate that
something that I did

00:08:35.413 --> 00:08:37.116
caused pain to another person.

00:08:37.182 --> 00:08:39.885
 Plus, it's loose.

00:08:39.951 --> 00:08:43.555
 I see Jay stepping
off the testing floor.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.524
I'm pretty sure this is it.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.726
This is it for me.

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:50.729
 Bladesmiths, in any one
of our finale competitions,

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.531
the way that you
design those blades

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.299
to perform in our
challenges is always

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:55.834
taken into consideration.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:58.737
And Robert,
unfortunately, your weapon

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:01.540
has hurt our user so
severely that we had to send

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.441
him to the emergency room.

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:05.043
Your weapon has
been given a vote

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.513
of no confidence and cannot
move forward in testing.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.315
And for that reason,
I have to ask

00:09:10.415 --> 00:09:12.018
you to please leave the forge.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:15.955
 First and
foremost, I hope that

00:09:16.021 --> 00:09:19.058
Jay doesn't suffer any long-term
effects of this injury.

00:09:19.124 --> 00:09:21.393
I took my time making
sure that everything

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.961
was safe on this blade.

00:09:23.028 --> 00:09:25.464
So to find out that I
missed something, that's

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:27.533
kind of devastating, you know?

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:30.402
I know that I'm able to
compete with some of the best

00:09:30.468 --> 00:09:32.271
bladesmiths here in the world.

00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:33.472
I know that this is my place.

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:35.141
This is my calling in life.

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:36.208
I'm certainly not going to stop.

00:09:36.309 --> 00:09:37.409
I'm going to keep
pushing forward.

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:39.111
I'm going to get
better at what I do.

00:09:39.177 --> 00:09:41.714
This is just another rung
on the ladder to success.

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:47.786
 Billy, your blade is
sharp, deadly, and strong,

00:09:47.853 --> 00:09:49.388
and you are the Forge
of Fire Champion.

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:52.491
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:52.557 --> 00:09:54.393
Good job, brother.

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:55.460
 Woo!

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.296
I'm the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:09:57.363 --> 00:09:59.398
This is awesome.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.066
This has been an
amazing experience,

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:04.269
and I'm very blessed and honored
to have been a part of it.

00:10:04.336 --> 00:10:05.602
[heavy metal music]

